{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790274826,"nonce":"S4pkkFLbqmgPR9FMAqFF7DE+wNQ=","title":"Lua: small semantic gaps found by the 5.4 audit","message":"At 8844ca79, both tiers, each against lua5.4: (1) goto f; local x; ::f:: print(x) is accepted where Lua refuses 'jumps into the scope of local'; (2) break cannot be followed by statements in the same block; (3) a generic for's fourth value (the closing value) is not closed when the loop breaks; (4) local c \u003cfoo\u003e with an unknown attribute; (5) an __index cycle aborts the process instead of raising \"'__index' chain too long; possible loop\"; (6) an exhausted gmatch iterator returns one nil instead of no values (select('#', it()) is 1, not 0); (7) runtime error messages ignore __name ('arithmetic on a table value' where lua5.4 says 'a MyType value'); (8) table.sort's comparison error has its operands swapped; (9) debug.traceback returns the message and a header with no frames. Reproducers are in the audit's scratch directory lua-state/ (lang, lang2, bugs); split into separate issues when fixing.","files":null}]}